PracticeChoicesTest
├── shuffle
│   ├── it moves items with a picker that says so
│   ├── it keeps every item exactly once
│   ├── it leaves the input untouched
│   ├── given a single item
│   │   └── it returns it unchanged
│   ├── given an empty list
│   │   └── it returns an empty list
│   └── given a picker that returns nonsense
│       └── it never drops an item
├── numericChoices
│   ├── it returns the requested number of options
│   ├── it includes the truth exactly once
│   ├── it spaces distractors multiplicatively
│   ├── it never renders two options identically
│   ├── it never offers a zero or negative option
│   ├── it puts the correct answer in different slots for different draws
│   ├── it numbers ids by final position
│   ├── when a format is given
│   │   └── it renders every option through it
│   ├── when a spread is given
│   │   └── it steps by that factor instead
│   ├── given a nonsense spread
│   │   └── it falls back to the default step
│   ├── given the draw picks the other direction first
│   │   └── it offers the smaller distractor first
│   ├── given a truth of zero or less
│   │   └── it refuses rather than inventing options
│   ├── given a truth that is not finite
│   │   └── it refuses
│   ├── given a count below two
│   │   └── it refuses
│   ├── given a count that is not a whole number
│   │   └── it refuses
│   ├── given more options than can be generated
│   │   └── it returns every distinct one that exists
│   ├── given a count that fills mid-pair
│   │   └── it stops rather than overshooting
│   ├── given offsets that overflow
│   │   └── it drops them
│   ├── given offsets that underflow to zero
│   │   └── it drops them
│   └── given a format that collapses every option
│       └── it refuses rather than asking a one-option question
└── labelledChoices
    ├── it offers every label once, with the correct id
    ├── it shuffles the labels
    ├── given duplicate labels
    │   └── it keeps the first and drops the rest
    ├── given the correct label is itself a duplicate
    │   └── it credits the surviving copy
    ├── given a correct index past the end
    │   └── it refuses
    ├── given a negative correct index
    │   └── it refuses
    ├── given a correct index that is not a whole number
    │   └── it refuses
    ├── given no labels
    │   └── it refuses
    └── given only one distinct label
        └── it refuses
